#: usr/bin/kiro-atelier-check:89
#, python-brace-format
msgid "Found: {cards}. "
msgstr ""

#: usr/bin/kiro-atelier-check:90
msgid "No NVIDIA card; painting needs one (AMD and Intel are not supported)."
msgstr ""

#: usr/bin/kiro-atelier-check:91
msgid ""
"Kiro Atelier paints with Stable Diffusion XL in ComfyUI, on PyTorch with "
"NVIDIA's CUDA. Intel graphics have no CUDA and share the normal memory, far "
"too slow and too small for SDXL. AMD cards would need PyTorch for ROCm, "
"which Kiro Atelier isn't built or tested for. No driver or setting changes "
"this: it takes an NVIDIA card (RTX 20xx / GTX 16xx or newer, 6 GB) in this "
"PC, or another Linux PC that has one."
msgstr ""

#: usr/bin/kiro-atelier-check:101
#, python-brace-format
msgid "Driver {version} is working."
msgstr ""

#: usr/bin/kiro-atelier-check:105
msgid "Not working, and current NVIDIA drivers no longer support this card."
msgstr ""

#: usr/bin/kiro-atelier-check:106
msgid ""
"NVIDIA's current drivers start at Turing (RTX 20xx / GTX 16xx); older cards "
"only work with legacy drivers, and even then the card would be too old for "
"Kiro Atelier (see Card generation)."
msgstr ""

#: usr/bin/kiro-atelier-check:108
msgid ""
"The NVIDIA driver is not working (not installed, or not loaded: restart). "
"Kiro Atelier's Setup can install it; run this check again afterwards."
msgstr ""

#: usr/bin/kiro-atelier-check:132
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Too old: {generation}. Kiro Atelier needs an RTX 20xx / GTX 16xx or newer."
msgstr ""

#: usr/bin/kiro-atelier-check:134
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"This card's compute capability is {cap}. The PyTorch build Kiro Atelier "
"installs (for CUDA 12.8) only contains code for compute 7.5 (Turing) and "
"newer, so it can't run anything on this card. An older PyTorch build still "
"supports it, but Kiro Atelier isn't built or tested for that."
msgstr ""

#: usr/bin/kiro-atelier-check:139
#, python-brace-format
msgid "Supported, but untested and likely slow: {generation}."
msgstr ""

#: usr/bin/kiro-atelier-check:141
msgid ""
"ComfyUI treats GTX 16xx and similar cards differently from RTX cards: by "
"default it doesn't use half precision (fp16) on them, the fast mode RTX "
"cards paint in. Expect painting to be clearly slower, and some settings may "
"not finish. Kiro Atelier hasn't been tested on these cards."
msgstr ""

#: usr/bin/kiro-atelier-check:144
#, python-brace-format
msgid "Supported: {generation} (compute {cap})."
msgstr ""

#: usr/bin/kiro-atelier-check:154
#, python-brace-format
msgid "{gb} GB, too little; painting needs at least {minimum} GB."
msgstr ""

#: usr/bin/kiro-atelier-check:156
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Kiro Atelier is built and tested for at least {minimum} GB of video memory. "
"ComfyUI has memory-saving modes that may run the painting model (SDXL) on "
"less, but slowly, and Kiro Atelier isn't tested that way; it can also run "
"out of memory."
msgstr ""

#: usr/bin/kiro-atelier-check:159 usr/bin/kiro-atelier-check:174
#, python-brace-format
msgid "{gb} GB."
msgstr ""

#: usr/bin/kiro-atelier-check:167
#, python-brace-format
msgid "{gb} GB; Kiro Atelier needs 16 GB."
msgstr ""

#: usr/bin/kiro-atelier-check:168
msgid ""
"While painting, ComfyUI keeps the SDXL model, the upscaler and the naming "
"model in normal memory next to the graphics card: about 10 GB. With less, "
"the PC swaps to disk or stops with an out-of-memory error."
msgstr ""

#: usr/bin/kiro-atelier-check:172
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"{gb} GB; it runs, but 16 GB is advised (expect swapping, close the browser "
"while painting)."
msgstr ""

#: usr/bin/kiro-atelier-check:181
#, python-brace-format
msgid "{gb} GB free in your home folder; about {needed} GB is needed."
msgstr ""

#: usr/bin/kiro-atelier-check:183
msgid ""
"ComfyUI and PyTorch take about 6 GB, the painting models (SDXL, its VAE, the "
"upscaler, the naming model) about 7.5 GB, and the paintings themselves need "
"room too."
msgstr ""

#: usr/bin/kiro-atelier-check:185
#, python-brace-format
msgid "{gb} GB free in your home folder."
msgstr ""

#: usr/bin/kiro-atelier-check:205
